{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Observation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Observation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Estimation?)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Estimation?)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Guessinggggggg)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Guessinggggggg)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular box has a total surface area of 94 square inches. The sum of the lengths of all its edges is 48 inches. What is the sum of the lengths in inches of all of its interior diagonals?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82de85ea2d09abbe0f316708bbb4e7a1f4f627e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 16\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"507\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side lengths of the rectangular box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \nFrom the information we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc86401a844711e88def93692937422d75fb2fea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(x+y+z) = 48 \\Rightarrow x+y+z = 12\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e781c0ada050703109cb29ab2e9696f544177b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(xy+yz+xz) = 94\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The sum of all the  lengths of the box's interior diagonals is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7e1a232129089dd72f040de7f6db3dad14b926.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 \\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Squaring the first expression, we get: \n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n144 =(x+y+z)^2 &amp;=  x^2+y^2+z^2 + 2(xy+yz+xz) \\\\\n&amp;=  x^2+y^2+z^2 + 94.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/84312496748f2bd8594ce025b657bf34646b97f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2+z^2 = 50\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/835d55911dfd8ed143f7905470abcd933e4bde66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 \\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2} =  \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\sqrt 2}\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Observation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Observation)\">Solution 2 (Observation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Observation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that a rectangular prism with side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827255dbd48aaf645900571ce04461a84082908a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> fits all the necessary conditions. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f98a1663c626f582ca6c86305eadf3e1b9297a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\sqrt{3^2+4^2+5^2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\sqrt 2}\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"33\" />\n~LuisFonseca123\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Estimation.3F.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Estimation?)\">Solution 3 (Estimation?)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Estimation?)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that a cube with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has an equal sum of edge lengths and a similar surface area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a292bfee2deea966779105c4694cf09466ec8051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(96)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" />. We can evaluate the total interior diagonal length of this cube to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580fa51087efd01969f8ad190ace7038c99fd137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Since the cube almost follows the problem's conditions, we can infer that the total interior diagonal length of the rectangular prism to be close but unequal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580fa51087efd01969f8ad190ace7038c99fd137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, which leads us to an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e6176d8e5cc60d386c7e357fe493026f19bc78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\sqrt 2}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Guessinggggggg.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Guessinggggggg)\">Solution 4 (Guessinggggggg)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Guessinggggggg)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that it just cannot be E, because this is way out of the others range. Next, observe that it cannot be B because it is not only pretty far away from C, but it is also the only one that is not divisible by 4. So we have 10, 16, 20 left. Note that the average of all the answers is highly skewed to the right of the median, therefore the answer will be around there (this is because the average of the answers is a good answer for MAA to use because it means that it is not obviously lower or higher than all 4 of the other answers, plus it is easier to get mislead with B or D.) With that being said, we can conclude that the answer is almost certainly D, because the average will be somewhat close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e6176d8e5cc60d386c7e357fe493026f19bc78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\sqrt 2}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of Ameri